<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21993" root="شذو" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَذَاةٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَذًا</span>, in three places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also <i>Sharpness.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And <i>Strength,</i> and <i>boldness,</i> of a
man. (Lth, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  [Or] <i>A remnant of strength:</i>
(S, K:) pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَذَوَاتٌ</span> (TA) and [coll. gen. n.] ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَذًا</span></b> .
(S, * TA. [See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَدًا</span>, in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شدو</span>.]) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  As an
epithet applied to a man, (TA,) <i>Evil in disposition,</i> (K, TA,) <i>sharp in temperament, that annoys,</i>
or <i>molests,</i> or <i>hurts, by his evil,</i> or <i>mischief:</i> in
some of the copies of the K, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الشَّىْءُ الخَلَقُ</span> is erroneously put for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">السَّىِّءُ الخُلُقِ</span>. (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  See
again <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَذًا</span>, last sentence.

